## build process in openshift

-- kubernetes alone can't deploy sourcecode, os thing

# buildconfig resource
-- configuration of the build
-- build is a result of buildconfig 
-- build strategies: docker build, source to image build, custom build

# docker build
oc new-app --name myapache https://github.com/... # public repo
-- use Dockerfile in that repo, openshift won't accept Containerfile :)

oc logs build/myapache-1 
-- alternative syntax -- some verbs take just a single parameter, so use / to merge resource and instance specification

# source to image build
-- if it can autotedtect the builder image, then it is as building from Dockerfile
-- if not, more specs are needed:

- try to define strategy
oc new-app --name myapache https://github.com/... --strategy=source
- define imagestream
oc new-app --name myapache python:3.8-ubi8~https://github.com/... 

- build scripts:
assemble, run, save-artifacts, usage

# managing application build 
oc new-app -- creates initial build config
oc start-build buildconfig/app
- starts the build
oc get builds
- see the build objects
oc cancel-build buildconfig/app

# troubleshooting build issues
- BUILD_LOGLEVEL env var to set the log level
oc set env buildconfig/app BUILD_LOGLEVEL="3"
oc logs build/app-1
- or use debug shell
oc debug deploy/app

# triggering builds
- image change triggers / webhook triggers
oc set triggers bc/name --from-image=project/image:tag
- from parameters, e.g. --from-image
- use --remove to cancel the trigger
oc set trigger deployment/name
- for apps deployed based on container
oc set triggers bc/name --from-gitlab
- using webhook trigger

- replacing exsting triggers, e.g.:
oc patch bc/name -p '{"spec": {"triggers": [{"type": "GitHub",
"github": {"secretReference": {"name": "github-trigger-secret"}}}]}}


